# Godot structure

Follow `docs/GODOT_PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md` when adding features.

- `Main` / `DungeonGame` only wires systems, camera, HUD paint, and input.
- Rules go in `scripts/game/` (`GameTypes`, `DungeonSim`, `RaidDirector`).
- 3D presentation stays in `scripts/world/` (`DungeonWorld`).
- Toolbar/HUD live in `scripts/hud/`.
- New scenes go under `scenes/`, not the repo root.
- Do not add new gameplay rules onto `scripts/Main.gd`.
- Communicate with signals where the HUD or world notifies the conductor.
- Do not duplicate `Tile` / `Tool` enums; use `GameTypes` or the `DungeonGame` aliases.
